+## TL;DR
+- `n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Flowise`, and `Langflow` are the strongest open source starting points for AI automation and internal workflows.
+- `Open WebUI`, `AnythingLLM`, `LibreChat`, and `PrivateGPT` are the most practical self-hosted AI workspaces for team knowledge, chat, and private assistants.
+- `Rasa`, `Botpress`, `Haystack`, and `Qdrant` are strong picks for customer support, retrieval, semantic search, and production-grade agent backends.
+- `Docling`, `Unstructured`, and `MarkItDown` are especially useful for small businesses trying to turn messy files into AI-ready content.
+- `InvokeAI`, `Stable Diffusion WebUI`, `Fooocus`, `Whisper`, and `faster-whisper` cover marketing images, audio transcription, and creative operations without SaaS lock-in.
+
+## Why This List
+Small teams need leverage, not another expensive black-box subscription. The best AI tools for small businesses in 2026 are increasingly open source: they can be self-hosted, audited, integrated into existing systems, and adapted to real workflows instead of forcing teams into proprietary product boundaries.
+
+This list intentionally excludes cloud-only proprietary SaaS products. If a tool did not have a public GitHub repository, it was not included.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Workflow Automation and Agent Platforms
+
+#### [n8n](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n)
+> **Description:** n8n describes itself as a fair-code workflow automation platform that combines visual building, custom code, self-hosting, native AI capabilities, and 400+ integrations. For small businesses, that translates into practical automations across lead capture, CRM sync, invoicing triggers, customer routing, and back-office tasks without buying a closed iPaaS product. The GitHub project is highly active and heavily adopted, which matters if you need community examples and deployment guides. GitHub metadata currently classifies its repo license as `Other`, reflecting n8n's fair-code licensing model rather than a standard SPDX open source tag.
