+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for small businesses in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting points are `n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, `Dify`, `Open WebUI`, `AnythingLLM`, and `Rasa`. The right choice depends on whether you need automation, document Q&A, customer support, or analytics.
+
+### Are these AI tools really open source and on GitHub?
+Yes. Every tool in this list has a public `github.com` repository. However, some repos use custom or fair-code licenses, and GitHub labels several of them as `Other` or `View license`, so you should review license terms before commercial deployment.
+
+### Which self-hosted AI tools are best for small business customer support?
+`Rasa`, `Botpress`, `Haystack`, `Qdrant`, `PrivateGPT`, and `Open WebUI` are strong starting points depending on whether you need structured workflows, semantic retrieval, private document access, or a broader self-hosted AI workspace.
+
+### Which GitHub AI repos are best for internal knowledge bases and document chat?
+`AnythingLLM`, `LibreChat`, `Open WebUI`, `PrivateGPT`, `Docling`, `Unstructured`, and `Dify` are especially useful for ingesting files and creating internal assistants over company documents.
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for small business marketing teams?
+`InvokeAI`, `Stable Diffusion WebUI`, `Fooocus`, `Whisper`, and `faster-whisper` are the most directly useful for image generation, ad concepts, transcription, and content repurposing.
+
+### Can a small business build AI workflows without proprietary SaaS?
+Yes. Repos like `n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, and `Dify` can be combined with open models, local document pipelines, and GitHub-native infrastructure to replace many proprietary workflow and AI app layers.
+
+### Why are some licenses listed as `Other` or `View license`?
+Because GitHub metadata for those repositories does not map cleanly to a standard SPDX short name. In those cases, the repo is still public on GitHub, but you should inspect the actual license text before production use.
